cad-open-relative-path-not-resolved-vs-cwd — (open "rel/path" ...) fails under clautolisp
==========================================================================================

Reported from: SCHMS+ loader generation (dev/lisp/make-loader.lsp) run
headless via `alfe --clautolisp --host mock`. clautolisp 1.7.x / alfe 1.7.x.

Symptom
-------

`(open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r")` — a path RELATIVE to the process
current working directory — returns NIL under clautolisp, even though
the file exists and the process cwd is the repo root. BricsCAD and
AutoCAD both resolve such a relative path against the current directory
and open it successfully (that is how SCHMS+ generates its loader today,
via `AUTOLISP_BIN --bricscad --mode batch`).

Repro
-----

    cd <repo>            # contains src-vlx/schmsplus.prj
    alfe --no-init --clautolisp --host mock \
         -x '(princ (list (open "src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r")))'
    => (nil)             ; clautolisp: relative path not found

    # absolute path works:
    alfe --no-init --clautolisp --host mock \
         -x '(princ (list (open "<repo>/src-vlx/schmsplus.prj" "r")))'
    => (#<file ...>)

Setting TRUSTEDPATHS to the repo subtree does NOT change the relative
case (so it is not a SECURELOAD gate — it is path resolution: the
relative name is never resolved against the process cwd).

Expected
--------

`open` (and by extension `findfile`, `load` given a bare relative name,
etc.) should resolve a relative path against the AutoLISP current
directory the same way BricsCAD/AutoCAD do — i.e. against the process
cwd in the headless `--clautolisp` host (or against a documented,
settable base). Today callers must pass absolute paths, which is awkward
for build tooling and forces absolute paths into generated artifacts
(a portability problem — such paths must not be committed).

Impact
------

SCHMS+ wants `schmsplus-loader.lsp` generated headless via clautolisp
(the clautolisp equivalent of the `.vlx`/`.des` CAD artifacts). The
generator opens the `.prj` and writes the loader; with only absolute
paths accepted, the generated loader would embed an absolute default
directory unless the generator is reworked to keep that default
relative. Native cwd-relative `open` would remove that friction.

Related: cad-path-dotdot-resolution.issue,
cad-vl-filename-directory-and-load.issue (other path-resolution
differences already filed).
